VINEYARD STABILITY INSIGHT:
  The observer's two gap-vines are ANTI-CORRELATED (ρ < 0).
  As g_left increases, g_right decreases (THM-387 flow).
  The stability theorem: vines are 1-Lipschitz (can't jump).

  Combined: the two vines MUST CROSS the threshold simultaneously.
  When vine_left is above threshold, vine_right is below (and vice versa).
  But at the TRANSITION (the 'vineyard crossing'), both are near threshold.
  The Lipschitz continuity ensures the crossing region has positive width.
  Within this region: both bars ≥ 1/(2n) → LONELY.

  This is the TOPOLOGICAL PROOF of LRC:
  anti-correlation + continuity + intermediate value theorem → crossing.

