PART 2: The annular braid — wrapping around the observer
======================================================================

n=4:
  total wraps: Σv = 6
  linking numbers: {1: 1, 2: 2, 3: 3}
  runner-runner crossings: 8
  observer-runner crossings: 12
  braid word length: 20

  ANNULAR STRUCTURE:
    the observer is the CORE (the hole in the annulus)
    runners can't pass THROUGH the observer — only AROUND
    lonely = all runners in the outer annular region
    the annular topology forces the linking sum to be nonzero:
    Σ link(obs, runner_i) = 6 ≠ 0

