ANNULAR DISENTANGLEMENT INSIGHT:
  Every LRC speed set has a positive disentanglement interval
  (confirmed at n=4,5,6). The observer strand always has a
  'straight' segment where no runner crossings occur.

  The disentanglement length measures the 'quality' of loneliness:
  longer disentanglement = more robust lonely interval.
  The initial segment has the SHORTEST disentanglement (wall-only,
  length ≈ 0). All other speed sets have longer disentanglements.

  In the annular braid group: the LRC trajectory's image always
  contains a 'trivial subword' (no observer crossings) of positive
  length. This is the BRAID-THEORETIC content of LRC.

======================================================================
GRAND SYNTHESIS
======================================================================

LRC through two topological lenses:

VINEYARD (persistence):
  The observer's two gap-bars trace anti-correlated vines.
  THM-387 forces the anti-correlation.
  The IVT forces a crossing where both bars ≥ 1/(2n) → lonely.
  The regular polygon is the UNIQUE crossing at g = 1/n exactly.

ANNULAR BRAID (topology):
  Runners wrap around the observer with linking number v_i.
  The total linking Σv = n(n-1)/2 is ALWAYS nonzero.
  But INSTANTANEOUS disentanglement (lonely time) exists because
  the geometric linking can temporarily vanish even though the
  algebraic linking is permanent.

THE DEEP CONNECTION:
  The vineyard crossing IS the annular disentanglement.
  When V_L = V_R at the threshold, the observer is momentarily
  'centered' in the annular gap — equidistant from both sides.
  This is the regular polygon configuration: maximum symmetry,
  minimum disentanglement width, but positive.

  The STABILITY THEOREM guarantees the crossing is robust:
  small perturbations of the speed set shift the crossing
  but don't destroy it. This is the TOPOLOGICAL CONTENT of LRC —
  the lonely time is a stable topological feature, not an accident.

